<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Yuan of Liang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">508–555</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Xiao Yi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Yuan of Liang, Xiao Yi, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-liang">Emperor Wu of Liang</a> and a noted scholar, crushed the rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hou-jing">Hou Jing</a> and took the throne at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangling">Jiangling</a> in 552. In 554 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-wei">Western Wei</a> armies captured Jiangling; the emperor burned the imperial library and was killed, and Western Wei installed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiao-cha">Xiao Cha</a> as ruler of the Western Liang.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-yuan-of-liang.jpg" alt="Emperor Yuan of Liang" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liang_Xiao_Yi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
